I've created a patch designed to optimize the tty port of NetHack for
terminals less than 80 characters wide.  I originally made this for
the Agenda VR3 port of NetHack 3.3.1 which ran in a small rxvt window.
 I recently got around to extracting these changes from the Agenda
port and applying them to the 3.4.2 source tree.  I don't know if
anyone has a use for this; I will personally be using it to play
NetHack on my Sharp Zaurus in a terminal window.

I've condensed the status bar information so that it takes-up less
room.  Ability scores except Charisma are abbreviated to 1 letter,
maximum values for hit points and power are not displayed, but an
asterisks is displayed if either stat is currently below the maximum
value.  Additionally, the "--More--" prompt for the message line at
the top of the window is replaced with a more concise ">>" prompt. 
Finally, the tombstone is condensed to a smaller size.

